  "goodToKnow": "Der Gummistiefel is a rubber boot or wellington: ein Paar Gummistiefel. They're standard for children in Kita, for farmers and at muddy festivals. Politicians in Gummistiefeln visiting flood areas became a symbol after the 2002 Elbe flood, when Gerhard Schröder's visit helped him win the election. Der Stiefel is a boot. The plural is the same: die Gummistiefel."
